#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# scorer_hi

#% text
# `scorer_hi(z)` gives the Scorer function `Hi(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `Hi(z)` is the integral of `exp(-t^3/3 + z t)` over `t > 0`, divided by `pi`; it solves `w'' - z w = 1/pi` (DLMF 9.12).

#% item
# `Hi(0) = 2 Bi(0)/3`; `Hi(x)` grows like `Bi(x)` as `x -> infinity` and tends to 0 like `-1/(pi x)` as `x -> -infinity`.

#% item
# Numerical values come from the Maclaurin series `3^(-2/3)/pi sum_k gamma((k + 1)/3) (3^(1/3) z)^k/k!`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
scorer_hi(3.0)
#% output
#= 13.923100094807092

#% cell
n(scorer_hi(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= 0.5301287993618319829747095496187327

#% cell
scorer_hi(0.2 + 1.0*im)
#% output
#= 0.30118043491810936 + 0.29018530779146345im

#% cell
scorer_hi(0)
#% output
#= 2*3^(5/6)/(9*gamma(2/3))

#% text
# `Gi + Hi = Bi`:

#% cell
scorer_gi(1.7) + scorer_hi(1.7) - airy_bi(1.7)
#% output
#= 0.0

